    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4): billing-integrity finding — the fare_breakdown line for the CTE (southbound) gantry after Braddell Road (SGD 2.00, charged 08:33) is a gantry this trip's GPS trace never passes (nearest fix 1,843.93 m away, well outside the 250 m match radius), and the booking route itemised ERP of SGD 0.00. The line is refunded in full as a standalone correction and is recorded here for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Both of you should read this the same way: the distance and time charges for the ride stand, the SGD 2.00 CTE ERP line comes off, and SGD 2.00 is refunded to the rider.\n\nWhat the trip shows. This is trip TRP-04006; the trip record, the GPS trace and the fare breakdown all carry that identifier and agree on the timestamps. The platform's booked optimal route from Ang Mo Kio Ave 6 to Novena Medical Center was 8.7 km (EV-TRIP-04006). The governing distance is the GPS trace figure of 9.84 km (EV-GPS-04006), not the rounded 9.8 km convenience copy on the trip record, because POL-RD-01 makes the trace figure govern. Excess = 9.84 - 8.7 = 1.14 km, which is 13.1% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only when the excess is greater than 20% of optimal AND greater than 0.8 km. The 13.1% fails the percentage test, so no route deviation is established, however the morning felt and whatever a usual fare has been.\n\nWhat follows for the contested amount. Because no deviation is established, POL-RD-02's optimal-route recomputation is never reached, and the distance charge (9.84 km x SGD 0.75 = SGD 7.38) and time charge (17 min x SGD 0.28 = SGD 4.76) stand as billed. The ledger reconciles to the cent: 3.80 base + 7.38 + 4.76 + 2.00 ERP + 0.80 platform fee = SGD 18.74 charged.\n\nThe one line that cannot stand. The SGD 2.00 ERP charge for the CTE (southbound) gantry after Braddell Road, charged at 08:33, is for a gantry the trace never passes: the closest of the 104 fixes, at 08:34:30, is 1,843.93 m from the gantry's recorded coordinates, far outside the 250 m radius POL-RD-09(4) treats as a crossing. The booking route itemised ERP of SGD 0.00, and the fare block itself marks the line as off the optimal route (SGD 2.00 off-optimal against SGD 0.00 on-optimal). Under POL-RD-09(4) a charge for a gantry the trace never crosses is a billing-integrity failure, refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists — and POL-RD-01 expressly preserves that limb where neither establishment test is met. Because no POL-RD-02 refund runs, nothing is double-counted (POL-RD-09(1)); and POL-RD-10(8) expressly excepts a line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), so this case is ruled rather than held.\n\nThe accounts of both parties. The driver's statement that he went by Upper Thomson and Thomson Road and never used the CTE agrees with the planned corridor on the record (Ang Mo Kio Ave 6, Ave 1, Marymount Rd, Thomson Rd, Sinaran Dr) and with the trace, which never approaches the gantry; it is consistent with the ruling but is not what carries it. The rider's account of a loop round Yio Chu Kang and '4-5 km extra' is supported by no artifact in the bundle and is contradicted by the only measurement on file (1.14 km, not 4-5 km); under POL-RD-08 an assertion unsupported by evidence carries no weight. The driver's submission that the rider's claim be met with NO_ACTION is rejected so far as it would leave the ERP line in place: the outcome is PARTIAL_REFUND on the rider's contested amount.\n\nPoints checked and not used as grounds. No traffic advisory exists in the bundle — EV-ADVIS-04006-01 is MISSING with weight_multiplier 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT — but neither party asserts an external traffic cause or cites that identifier, so under POL-RD-13 there is nothing to test against it, POL-RD-03 is simply unavailable, and no POL-RD-10(5) escalation arises. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07(a) to (c): 104 fixes at a 10 s cadence, largest interval 10 s, largest straight-line step 114.0 m, highest implied speed 41.0 km/h. So the gap consequences of POL-RD-07 and POL-RD-10(3) do not engage, and the absence of any CTE crossing is a real absence rather than a hole in the record. POL-RD-06's driver_profile check is not triggered, the deviation being neither established nor material, and consulted anyway it returns nothing: deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 295 completed trips in 90 days, so no FULL_REFUND uplift and no driver-conduct referral. The remaining profile fields mentioned on both sides (rating, lifetime_trips, prior_deviation_flags, prior_disputes_filed) are context only under POL-GEN-01 and ground nothing here. POL-RD-04's compensation limb is not available: the billed distance (9.84 km) is not less than the trace distance, so there is no unbilled distance to pay for, and driver_compensation_sgd is null.\n\nAmount and confidence. Contested SGD 6.00; refunded SGD 2.00, being the CTE ERP correction alone. Confidence is 0.9: the artifacts the ruling rests on — EV-GPS-04006, EV-TRIP-04006 and EV-FARE-04006 — all carry weight_multiplier 1.0, so the POL-GEN-02(2) cap is 1.0 and the 0.70 floor is nowhere near. The monetary effect (SGD 2.00) is below the SGD 8.00 execution threshold, so under POL-GEN-05 it executes automatically on issue; either party may appeal under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "PARTIAL_REFUND",
    "amount_sgd": 2.0,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": null,
    "referrals": [
      "POL-RD-09(4) billing-integrity referral: fare breakdown EV-FARE-04006 charges SGD 2.00 for the CTE (southbound) gantry after Braddell Road (charged 08:33:00), a gantry the trip's GPS trace EV-GPS-04006 never passes — the nearest of the 104 fixes is 1,843.93 m away (index 76, 08:34:30), far outside the 250 m radius POL-RD-09(4) treats as a crossing. The line has been refunded in full as a standalone pass-through correction; refer the ERP posting for billing-integrity review."
    ],
    "confidence": 0.9,
    "explanation": "Rider: you were right about one line and it has been refunded — SGD 2.00. Driver: the rest of the fare stands, and neither of you is at fault for the rest.\n\nDISTANCE AND TIME — NO REFUND. Trip TRP-04006 ran from Ang Mo Kio Ave 6 to Novena Medical Center. Under POL-RD-01 the governing measurement is the GPS trace EV-GPS-04006, not the rounded convenience copy on the trip record: the trace measures 9.84 km against a booked optimal of 8.7 km (EV-TRIP-04006). The excess is 1.14 km, which is 13.10% of optimal. POL-RD-01 establishes a deviation only where the excess is BOTH more than 20% of the optimal distance AND more than 0.8 km. The absolute limb passes, but the percentage limb fails by a wide margin, so no route deviation is established on this trip, however the morning felt and however the trip was characterised. Your estimate of '4-5 km extra' is not supported by anything in the bundle — the only measurement on file shows roughly a quarter of that — and the route the platform recorded at booking (Ang Mo Kio Ave 6, Ave 1, Marymount Rd, Thomson Rd, Sinaran Dr) is the ordinary AMK-to-Novena corridor, consistent with the driver's account that he used Upper Thomson and Thomson Road. No evidence supports a loop round Yio Chu Kang.\n\nBecause no deviation is established, the POL-RD-02 recomputation never runs and no recomputed fare is produced; there is therefore no distance or time refund. The metered lines stand exactly as billed: base fare SGD 3.80, distance 9.84 km at SGD 0.75 = SGD 7.38, time 17 min at SGD 0.28 = SGD 4.76, platform fee SGD 0.80; charged_total SGD 18.74 (EV-FARE-04006), payment status CHARGED, nothing refunded so far. The trace is not impaired for policy purposes under POL-RD-07: 104 fixes at a 10-second cadence from 08:21:50 to 08:38:57, largest interval 10 s, largest step 114 m, no sustained sampling above 30 s — so the 1.14 km figure is sound, no independent corroboration is required, and nothing escalates on trace integrity.\n\nTHE ERP LINE — REFUNDED. The one line that does not survive is the SGD 2.00 charge for the CTE (southbound) gantry after Braddell Road (EV-FARE-04006, charged 08:33:00 at 1.3412, 103.8559). POL-RD-09(4) matches a gantry to the trace by treating any fix within 250 m as a crossing. The closest approach on the whole trace is 1,843.93 m (fix 76, 08:34:30), and no pair of fixes brackets a closer approach. The vehicle never crossed that gantry. The platform's own booking route itemised ERP of SGD 0.00, the fare breakdown itself records the gantry as off-optimal (SGD 2.00 off-optimal against SGD 0.00 on-optimal), and the driver's own statement accepts the charge was not his ('Never go CTE. The ERP charge not from me.'). That is a billing-integrity failure: it is refunded in full as a standalone correction, available whether or not a deviation exists, and it is not added on top of anything — no POL-RD-02 refund runs, so there is no double counting.\n\nOTHER POINTS. No traffic advisory was on file: EV-ADVIS-04006-01 is MISSING with weight 0.0 and issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT, so POL-RD-03 is simply unavailable. Neither party asserted an external traffic cause (a closure, a queue, a breakdown), so nothing was invoked against the missing artifact and its absence is a gap in the bundle, not a contradiction — under POL-RD-13 it neither reduces the excess nor escalates the case, and no POL-RD-10(5) trigger fires. No other POL-RD-10 trigger fires either: the trip identifier matches across the trip record, trace and fare breakdown, the timestamps are causally ordered and the trace's first and last fixes equal started_at and ended_at to the second, the refund is far under the SGD 150.00 ceiling, and the only unmatched charge line is the ERP line refunded under POL-RD-09(4), which POL-RD-10(8) expressly excepts. This case is decided, not held.\n\nDRIVER CONDUCT AND COMPENSATION. POL-RD-06 is not engaged: the deviation is neither established nor material (materiality needs over 50% of optimal or over 8.0 km). Consulted anyway, it returns the same answer — deviation_flags_90d is 0 against 295 completed trips in 90 days, so no pattern exists, no FULL_REFUND uplift applies and no driver-conduct referral is made. The other profile fields mentioned in the arguments — rating, lifetime_trips, prior_deviation_flags, prior_disputes_filed, acceptance_rate, account_age_days — are context only under POL-GEN-01, no finding rests on them, and they were not used. No driver compensation is due: the rider was billed for the full 9.84 km the trace records, so POL-RD-04's unbilled-distance limb has no shortfall to work on.\n\nFIGURES USED. Charged total SGD 18.74 (EV-FARE-04006); refund to the rider SGD 2.00 (the ERP line); driver compensation nil; the SGD 12.14 of distance and time charges earned on this trip stand. The monetary effect is below the SGD 8.00 automatic-execution threshold, so the SGD 2.00 is released on issue. This ruling was made without human review; either party may appeal once within 30 days under POL-GEN-04."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
